-- 9. WHAT THIS LOG DOES NOT SETTLE -----------------------------------------------
#   * Which way the phone really was at second 385 of that boot. Nothing recorded it.
#   * Whether the accelerometer's x and y axes are where this stack expects them. That
#     is now the ONLY remaining candidate for "the screen sits landscape", and it is a
#     one-hand measurement (see docs 92): hold the phone upright in portrait and read
#     the sensorfw value. If it reads 4 (BottomDown) the axes are fine; if it reads 1 or
#     2 the x/y pair is wrong; if it reads 3 the pair is inverted.
#   * Whether sensorfw actually delivers a new value when the phone is moved (docs 71
#     section 7.5 observed no orientationChanged in 30 s, but the phone was flat and
#     still for that whole test, where no change is expected -- so that observation is
#     not evidence either way).
#   * Nothing here was run on the device. It is all host-side, read-only.
